from a double-digit-failure first week to a single failure in its last five weeks and none in its
last 20 days, and the trajectory is visible only because the heartbeat rows exist. As a claim about
silence: we do not claim the system did not fail; we claim that within its enumerated failure modes
it could not fail without leaving a record, and that not one of the 85 recorded failures was
discovered by suspicion or archaeology.
4.2
The instrumented window: ten days at full resolution
The 2026-08-19 →08-28 window (ten calendar days, bounded by the precision instrument’s deploy-
ment date on one side and this draft on the other) adds denominator-complete injection telemetry.
It was a light-duty period by the project’s standards (2,121 hook invocations, roughly a sixth of the
lifetime daily average, spanning a multi-day idle gap and a network outage), which bounds what it
can show about load, though not about precision.
Turn taxonomy, defined once: a prompt is any UserPromptSubmit event (68 in the window;
every one writes a telemetry row). Prompts divide into machine-generated turns (agent-completion
callbacks and similar mechanical events) and human-authored turns; independently, the intent
detector marks 14 prompts intent-bearing (build/investigate/decide). Five injection firings on the
deployment day were authors’ synthetic validation probes and are excluded from use-analysis by
that stated rule; they appear in the appendix.
Under the old pre-gate behavior (the stale-claim block firing on roughly four in five intent-bearing
prompts), a 14-intent-prompt window would have produced on the order of eleven noise firings. The
instrumented window produced three, all judged relevant, and zero on the 54 non-intent prompts.
We present the old rate as recorded context (its sample denominator was not preserved); the
window’s own denominator is complete, and the adjudication of "topically justified" is the authors’,
a construct-validity limit stated in §6.
